title: Refresh list request sent during a new handshake is taken for one of the start's
  own
updated: 2026-11-06T13:16:06Z
---

Found during k106. Http.pm classifies a non-call request as a start's own while {handshake} is set. A tools/list / prompts/list / resources/list from an operator refresh (refresh_p) that is sent while a new handshake runs is therefore taken for the start's: a stop cuts it off, and it goes out on the half-open session. Effect is only debug-logged and only operator-triggered. A precise fix needs Upstream.pm (_handshake_p / _list_all_p) to mark its own requests, e.g. pass a flag down to request_p -- outside Http.pm.

Fixed: _handshake_p passes $of_start down _list_all_p/_paginate_p to _request_p; Http no longer guesses from {handshake}/method name (both removed). Test in t/http.t, in-loop (start goes through / stop calls it off), red on HEAD 6/29. Committed as 153f03d.
